"Correct is B: it teaches in the right shape (story \u2192 inversion \u2192 finite list \u2192 their role), speaks plainly, and empowers \u2014 the teaching performance the culture question tests. A is wrong: rule taxonomy at a first-week tech is the lecture, not the lesson. C is wrong: 'read the docs' is the abdication of teaching. D is wrong: outsourcing the teaching to the bootcamp dodges the question you were asked.",
