[["The read", "In Florida, non-competes have teeth \u2014 and this one's scope ('any endpoint security employer,' 100 miles from Orlando) could fence you out of your own industry. This is the line that matters most in the offer."],
["The move", "Raise it professionally BEFORE signing: 'I want to flag the non-compete's scope \u2014 12 months across endpoint security within 100 miles would prevent me working in my field here. Can we narrow it to [specific competitors / shorter term]?' Negotiate the clause like the compensation \u2014 it IS compensation (of your future)."],
["The backstop", "Concerning clauses get professional review before signing. Never sign a career-fencing clause hoping it won't be enforced."]],
"12-month, 100-mile, 'any endpoint security employer.' Sign?",
