"Correct is B: the specific, grabbable offer made directly, no fanfare, no credit-seeking \u2014 help that doesn't burden the drowning person with asking. A is wrong: 'let me know' is the offer that never gets taken (the burden stays on them). C is wrong: reporting the struggle to the manager skips the peer-level help entirely. D is wrong: 'not my queue' is the anti-teammate.",
